{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_health.py","reason":"store_status() reports {path,present,expected}; run_startup_store_sweep() extracted here (same store-visibility concern, and keeps mcp_server under the module-size cap) and emits a WARNING naming the path when the store is absent"},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"Boot calls run_startup_store_sweep instead of inlining the sweep"},{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"Readiness gate refuses to promote a container reporting expected-but-absent store (mcp-store-missing), keyed on expected so it is inert until a tracker dir is configured"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py","reason":"store_status behavior: absent+expected, present, not-expected, never raises; and the gate predicate"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py","reason":"The /health payload gained a store field; keep the exact in_flight assertions and pin the new key"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_tombstone_registry.py","reason":"The boot sweep moved, so the RemovedInputError contract check now scans the boot-path module set"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py","reason":"Drive the store gate through the harness: refuses when expected+absent, promotes when not expected, promotes when /health predates the field"}]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1787728013762757001,"uuid":"a78a9f91-f65c-415e-a70b-167cfb074b6c"}